{"name":"Snowball Effect","hex":"#d9e9e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowball effect","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An accelerating growth of magnitude, including fame, fortune, importance, or danger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowball_effect"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowball effect","blocks":[{"text":"A snowball effect is a process that starts from an initial state of small significance and builds upon itself, becoming larger, and also perhaps potentially more dangerous or disastrous, though it might be beneficial instead. This is a cliché in cartoons and modern theatrics, and it is also used in psychology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/A_Russian_Ball_-_DPLA_-_a96db3c821ad3287ca68e6432f1ce673_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-A_Russian_Ball_-_DPLA_-_a96db3c821ad3287ca68e6432f1ce673_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowball_effect"},{"title":"Snowball Effect (equity crowdfunding)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowball Effect is a New Zealand-based online investing marketplace, that enables New Zealand companies to offer shares to members of the public.\nSnowball Effect launched in August 2014, after being one of the first to acquire an equity crowdfunding license from the Financial Markets Authority. As of November 2020 over NZ$75 million has been raised on the platform."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowball_Effect_(equity_crowdfunding)"},{"title":"Snowball","blocks":[{"text":"A snowball is a spherical object made from snow, usually created by scooping snow with the hands and pressing the snow together to compact it into a ball. Snowballs are often used in games such as snowball fights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/%D0%A1%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B6%D0%BE%D0%BA1.jpg/330px-%D0%A1%D0%BD%D0%B5%D0%B6%D0%BE%D0%BA1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp